  "id": "COMPOUND:36759 - PROTEIN:2271",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 1-Tridecene-3,5,7,9,11-pentayne may interact with V-type sodium ATPase subunit K. This compound is implicated in the target pathway through mRNA interferase EndoA, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Alsterpaullone and Indirubin-3'-monoxime. These latter two agents are known to inhibit the V-type sodium ATPase subunit K, a critical enzyme involved in maintaining cellular ion homeostasis. The shared target of 1-Tridecene-3,5,7,9,11-pentayne and these compounds suggests a possible mode of action involving the inhibition of the sodium pump, potentially through a common target or a similar molecular mechanism. The evidence is supported by the presence of a direct interaction between the compound and the target subunit, as indicated by the path scores, which reflect a plausible and consistent relationship across multiple pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that 1-Tridecene-3,5,7,9,11-pentayne may act as a modulator of the V-type sodium ATPase subunit K, possibly by interfering with its function in cellular processes.",
